Error [jet.InvalidOsDispatchArm]: `.Bsd` is not an OS arm — a `#build.target.os` dispatch arm names OSes of the `OS` list, such as `.Linux` or `.Web | .Wasm`
  --> Tests/UI/os_target_dispatch_bad_arm.jet:6:9
    |
  6 |         .Bsd -> { print("bsd") }
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Each arm gates code for the OSes it names, so its head is a bare, payload-free OS variant or an or-pattern of them — the same list `#Target(OS.*)` uses — and each OS appears at most once
 Fix: Name each OS in one arm, such as `.Linux -> …` or `.Web | .Wasm -> …`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-OSTARGET-DISPATCH-ARM
